{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/api/books?bibkeys=OLID:OL25849067M,OLID:OL26195223M,OLID:OL27203735M,OLID:OL27404915M,OLID:OL27538561M,OLID:OL28200792M,OLID:OL39603048M,OLID:OL40433466M,OLID:OL40478233M,OLID:OL43020294M,OLID:OL43657047M,OLID:OL45738827M,OLID:OL51296984M,OLID:OL52887341M,OLID:OL59698440M&jscmd=details&format=json","file":"data/metadata3000_261025/raw/library-9c4b0c0975c5042e.json","retrieved":"2026-10-25T22:10:59.881Z","status":200,"data":{"OLID:OL25849067M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL25849067M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25849067M/Google","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/howgoogleworks0000schm","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7898991-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Grand Central Publishing"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["20549458"]},"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Introduction: Lessons learned from the front row : \"Just go talk to the engineers\" ; The Finland plan ; When astonishing isn't ; Speed ; The \"smart creative\" ; A fun project for the two of us ; Pyramids unbuilt","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Culture: believe your own slogans : Keep them crowded ; Work, eat, and live together ; Your parents were wrong, messiness is a virtue ; Don't listen to the HiPPOs ; The rule of seven ; Every tub (not) on its own bottom ; Do all reorgs in a day ; The Bezos two-pizza rule ; Organize the company around the people whose impact is the highest ; Exile knaves but fight for divas ; Overworked in a good way ; Establish a culture of yes ; fun, not Fun ; You must wear something ; Ah'cha'rye ; Don't be evil","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Strategy: your plan is wrong : Bet on technical insights, not market research ; A period of combinatorial innovation ; Don't look for faster horses ; Optimize for growth ; Coase and the nature of the firm ; Specialize ; Default to open, not closed ; Default to open, except when ... ; Don't follow competition ; Eric's notes for a strategy meeting","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Talent: hiring is the most important thing you do : The herd effect ; Passionate people don't use the word ; Hire learning animals ; The LAX test ; Insight that can't be taught ; Expand the aperture ; Everyone knows someone great ; Interviewing is the most important skill ; Schedule interviews for thirty minutes ; Have an opinion ; Friends don't let friends hire (or promote) friends ; Urgency of the role isn't sufficiently important to compromise quality in hiring ; Disproportionate rewards ; Trade the M & Ms, keep the raisins ; If you love them, let them go (but only after taking these steps) ; Firing sucks ; Google's hiring dos and don'ts ; Career: choose the F-16 ; Treat your career like you are surfing ; Always listen for those who get technology ; Plan your career ; Statistics is the new plastics ; Read ; Know your elevator pitch ; Go abroad ; Combine passion with contribution","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Decisions: the true meaning of consensus : Decide with data ; Beware the bobblehead yes ; Know when to ring the bell ; Make fewer decisions ; Meet every day ; \"You're both right\" ; Every meeting needs an owner ; Horseback law ; Spend 80 percent of your time on 80 percent of your revenue ; Have a succession plan ; The world's best athletes need coaches, and you don't?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Communications: be a damn good router : Default to open ; Know the details ; It must be safe to tell the truth ; Start the conversation ; Repetition doesn't spoil the prayer ; How was London? ; Review yourself ; Email wisdom ; Have a playbook ; Relationships, not hierarchy","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Innovation : create the primordial ooze : What is innovation? ; Understand your context ; The CEO needs to be the CIO ; Focus on the user ... ; Think big ; Set (almost) unattainable goals ; 70/20/10 ; 20 percent time ; Jonathan's favorite 20 percent project ; Ideas come from anywhere ; Ship and iterate ; Fail well ; It's not about money","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Conclusion: Imagine the unimaginable : From Downton Abbey to Diapers.com ; Who succeeds and who fails in a world of platforms? ; The emergence of the social web (and a start-up called Facebook) ; Ask the hardest questions ; The role of government ; Big problems are information problems ; The future's so bright ... ; The next smart creative.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"weight":"1.1 pounds","covers":[7898991,7381110],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223108260754","urn:sfpl:31223108260135","urn:sfpl:31223108260739","urn:sfpl:31223108260762","urn:sfpl:31223108260127","urn:sfpl:31223108260747","urn:sfpl:31223108253098","urn:sfpl:31223108260770","urn:sfpl:31223108260150","urn:sfpl:31223108260721","urn:sfpl:31223108260119"],"physical_format":"Hardcover","key":"/books/OL25849067M","publish_places":["New York"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"xiv, 286 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run05.mrc:67205608:5406","ia:howgoogleworks0000schm","bwb:9781455582341","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part41.utf8:164846309:2528","ia:howgoogleworks0000schm_o6d9","amazon:1455582344","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.14.20150123.full.mrc:237173856:3437","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-025.mrc:28198705:6972","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:115226659:5926"],"title":"Google","notes":"Includes bibliographical references and index.","number_of_pages":286,"edition_name":"1st ed.","subtitle":"how Google works","publish_date":"2014","by_statement":"Eric Schmidt and Jonathan Rosenberg, with Alan Eagle.","works":[{"key":"/